o nearby tiles to form sequences, (2) Only 1 copy remains unshown, making it nearly impossible to use, (3) It doesn't contribute to any scoring patterns. Discarding T2 maintains the best hand structure with W1-W2-W3 chow, W4 pung, B1-B2-B3-B4 flexibility, and F1 pair.\n\nAnswer: Play T2"}
